82:**Nest clips can't be pasted.** The clipboard holds the nest clip but not what's inside it, so **Paste** shows an error and pastes nothing, even if only one of the copied clips is a nest clip. **Cut** still deletes a nest clip, so press <kbd>⌘Z</kbd> to bring it back. To make another copy of a nest clip, use [Duplicate or ⌥-drag](/editing/duplicate-clips/).
85:- A paste lands whole or not at all. If one clip can't go in, Frame Job shows an error naming it and nothing changes. An [adjustment clip](/color/adjustment-clips/), for example, can't be pasted while a [nest](/editing/nests/) is open.
87:- Copy and Paste work inside a nest. **Copy** takes the clips you picked and counts their depth against the nest's own tracks, and **Paste** lands in the nest that's open.
91:`paste` takes a description of the clips in the same form Copy writes, so an agent can place clips without touching your clipboard, at any time and on any track. See [Tools: copy and nest](/mcp/tools-copy-and-nest/).

